#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069972 :tutorial/content "Multiplying rational expressions is just like multiplying fractions. After all, fractions are just rational expressions with constants!\n\nFor example, to multiply the rational expressions $\\dfrac{3}{x}$ and $\\dfrac{y}{2},$ we multiply the numerators and the denominators as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\cdot \\dfrac{y}{2} = \\dfrac{3 \\cdot y}{x \\cdot 2} = \\dfrac{3y}{2x}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "9b51617b-96b7-5112-bd91-a351a05ee49a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3378 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
